    "summary": "gh-922 suite tests fail under the dart shard harness (disposable-copy git ops)",
    "description": "**Evidence (epam/dmtools-dart quality, waves 17:47Z + 18:18Z 2026-10-16):** the two new tests from #923 fail when the agents suite runs under dart's suite_shard_runner: ```❌ smAgent: trigger fail-open dispatch (gh-922) > a multi-line [marker flattening]`` `❌ ... > two rules fa[il-open ordering]`` — 713 passed / 2 failed, agents-gate red (dart PR #414 blocked on it). Same tests green in this repo's own CI.

**Suspect:** the log around the failures carries `Could not checkout expected branch, using current: deve...` — the tests appear to perform real git checkouts, which break inside dart's disposable suite copies (the .git is an absolute gitfile ref into the original tree — checkout of another branch is impossible by design). Run: https://github.com/epam/dmtools-dart/actions/runs/$(the 18:18Z ai/gh-384 quality wave), shard 2/6.

**Ask:** make the gh-922 tests hermetic (no real branch checkouts — fixture state only), or gate the git-dependent path behind the same isolation guards the other lifecycle tests use.

